          <Pad Id="IwIxy87zQ3aLD8GXxEtKGf" Comment="" Bounds="1393,1171,35,49" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Pad Id="FZtbP03kzOAP6HYGHgrMWO" Bounds="716,1004,475,485" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="SweepCast is a raycast with volume: instead of an infinitely thin line, a whole shape travels from Origin along Direction, and you get the closest point where that moving shape would first touch something. The Shape pin picks Sphere (default), Box or Capsule; Radius / Box Size / Capsule Length size it (only the pins matching the chosen shape are used) and Orientation rotates it, which matters for boxes and capsules. The hit's Distance is how far the shape travels before contact - world units, same as RayCast - and the hit point/normal is where the surfaces touch, which unlike a raycast can be off the center line, anywhere within the shape's cross-section.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Typical uses are &quot;will this fit / where would it land&quot; questions:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Camera collision: sweep a small sphere from the player toward the camera position; place the camera at the hit distance so it never clips into walls.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Movement pre-check: before teleporting or moving a crate, sweep its box shape along the intended path, the closest hit tells you how far it can actually go.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Thick projectiles: a cannonball or snowball is a sphere sweep, and it correctly clips things a thin ray would miss by a hair.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Ground probing: sweeping the character's own sphere downward gives a landing point that accounts for the body's width, where a center raycast might slip through a gap.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="Doi399d38yKN16bIWnM8os" Bounds="1817,1004,451,271" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="SweepCastPenetrating is to SweepCast what RayCastPenetrating is to RayCast: it doesn't stop at the first contact but reports every collidable the swept shape would touch along the full Max Distance, as a Spread&lt;HitInfo&gt;. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Use it when you want the complete list rather than the nearest blocker:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Everything a swinging blade or shockwave volume passes through in one motion.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;All obstacles blocking a corridor of a given width (sweep a box of that width and enumerate).&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Everything a thick beam weapon pierces, with per-hit points and normals for placing effects.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
